    secId: "qii3-DI-section9",
    content:
      "Further Reading on Decarbonizing Infrastructure If you’d like to dive deeper, these resources provide detailed methodologies, frameworks, and tracking tools relevant to infrastructure decarbonization. Global: Greenhouse Gas Protocol A widely used international accounting standard for greenhouse gas emissions, developed by WRI and WBCSD. Provides comprehensive global standardized frameworks to measure and manage GHG emissions, with sector-specific and country-specific calculation tools for private and public sector operations, value chains, and mitigation actions. Global: RICS Whole Life Carbon Assessment Standard Professional standard from the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors for measuring carbon emissions across the entire lifecycle of built assets, from raw material extraction through construction, operation, and end of life. Global: Reducing Infrastructure Climate Risk Through Technology Measures Guidance on developing decarbonization roadmaps for infrastructure owners and investors. The initiative identifies and evaluates over 100 decarbonization and climate resilience strategies across 101 infrastructure asset subclasses, resulting in more than 1,800 unique asset-strategy applications. Each strategy is assessed for effectiveness and hazard protection level (for physical risks).",
